{"body":"Rel: #12
Ref: #2
Implementation: PR #17

## Decision

Environment固有の実値はownerがGit commitせずGitHub Environmentへ入力し、Gitは名前・型・lifecycle・責務・検査規則だけを保持する。

```text
Git
└─ required name / type / lifecycle / ownership / validation

GitHub Environment Variables
└─ owner-managed non-secret values

GitHub Environment Secrets
└─ owner-managed secret values

Git / SOPS
└─ workflow-generated durable ciphertext authority
```

## Current canonical mapping

| Environment | Secrets | Variables |
|---|---|---|
| `dev-authoring` | `JEV_API_KEY` | `SOPS_AGE_RECIPIENTS` |
| `dev-projection` | `SOPS_AGE_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` |
| `stg-projection` | `JEV_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` |
| `prd-projection` | `JEV_API_KEY`, `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` | `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` |

There are no stg/prd authoring Environments.

## Completion readback

PR #17 merged into `proposals` as `e95d591256c614419ba0a026ea78cf97397547ed`.

Confirmed source outcome:

- `SOURCE_JEV_API_KEY` alias removed;
- Git stores no `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` or `SOPS_AGE_RECIPIENTS` live value;
- authoring requires `JEV_API_KEY` secret + `SOPS_AGE_RECIPIENTS` variable;
- projection requires the contract-declared Environment inputs;
- missing/invalid input becomes RED before provider effect;
- source contract, workflow, adapter, tests and README agree on value placement;
- owner bootstrap for dev inputs was performed separately and recorded without values in PR #17;
- merge-after CI on `proposals` passed.

## Physical lifecycle handoff

The following is intentionally **not** a remaining DoD of this design/source Issue:

```text
real authoring
→ durable ciphertext merge
→ owner deletes one-shot dev-authoring/JEV_API_KEY
```

That is physical cutover state owned/tracked by #2. The envs workflow does not delete Environment inputs; deletion is a separate owner effect.

Likewise, #18 must close before real authoring/projection dispatch so source Green is not promoted to an unowned executable effect entry.

## Done

- [x] Environment Variables/Secrets are the value SSOT;
- [x] Git contains only names/types/lifecycles/validation plus generated ciphertext;
- [x] dev authoring variable and secret names are canonical;
- [x] projection variable/secret names are canonical;
- [x] missing/invalid inputs fail before provider effect;
- [x] source/workflow/tests/docs agree;
- [x] owner bootstrap evidence is recorded without values;
- [x] physical one-shot deletion is explicitly handed to #2 rather than falsely claimed here.

## Non-goals

- executing real authoring/projection;
- deleting Environment inputs from envs workflow;
- activating stg/prd;
- declaring consumer runtime PASS."}

