## Product-completion gates

The proof must preserve every requirement documented in the handoff:

- final current flake builds without changing its lock;
- offline `--no-write-lock-file` rebuild resolves to the same output path;
- final store path, recursive closure, closure size, symlink targets, and binary SHA-256 values are retained;
- Vim reports `9.2.0478`, terminal support, and the required features;
- the runtime closure has no GTK/X11/Python/Ruby/Lua dependency;
- `proof-sh` is a regular file and its digest is bound in the executable-binding registry;
- `TestCanonicalHQVimConformance` passes on the final minimal output;
- `TestNativeHQFuzzyAutomaticPopupDoesNotAccept` passes all schema-template, field-key, and Unicode/CRLF journeys inside a fresh Herdr PTY;
- process evidence binds Vim to the exact HQ `lsp --profile local` executable;
- one workspace has exactly two panes, with layout/focus/read/process evidence;
- the finite world contains only the harmless `@proof.echo` local tool;
- real Vim submission appends exactly one accepted instruction;
- the corresponding result sequence is exactly `accepted → started → stdout → completed` with stdout/final text `hq-vim-e2e-ok` and one run/instruction identity;
- worker health is ready before submission;
- cleanup uses the typed worker stop path, closes the workspace/session, and leaves no proof process;
- no provider-side log unsupported by the pinned HQ commit is required.

## OCI/WSLC projection

OCI is an additional distribution and independent runtime surface for the same completed Nix closure. It is not a second product implementation.

Required outputs:

```text
vim-nix-herdr-hq.docker.tar
vim-nix-herdr-hq.oci.tar
OCI index / manifest / config / layer digest receipt
Docker-runtime proof receipt
OCI-runtime proof receipt
WSLC-TEST.md
SHA256SUMS
source ZIP
exact Git bundle
```

CI must load and run the Docker archive, convert it with pinned Nixpkgs Skopeo, load the OCI projection independently, run the same full proof again, and compare the semantic receipts. A successful image build without the inner PTY/HQ/worker proof is not completion.

The downloadable pack is intended for user-side WSLC execution and feedback. User-side results may request further iterations; no final bundle is labeled complete until both CI proof and the documented completion gates are Green.

## Fail-closed cases

At minimum reject:

1. lock mutation;
2. output-path drift between normal and offline build;
3. incomplete runtime closure;
4. wrong Vim/HQ/Herdr/client version;
5. forbidden GUI/language runtime dependency;
6. symlinked or digest-mismatched `proof-sh`;
7. popup test timeout or partial subtest success;
8. process evidence missing exact HQ path/profile;
9. pane count other than two;
10. missing worker-ready state;
11. zero or multiple accepted instructions;
12. missing, reordered, duplicated, or failed result event;
13. wrong stdout/final text;
14. provider identity mismatch;
15. residual worker/Herdr/Vim/HQ process;
16. malformed or digest-mismatched OCI descriptor/blob;
17. Docker-only Green with OCI replay absent;
18. OCI-only shell smoke substituted for the full product proof;
19. artifact upload response treated as runtime readback;
20. final-bundle claim before all gates pass.

## Relationship to ops

- `ops#187` supplies the proven pinned-Nixpkgs/OCI materialization pattern.
- `ops#188` owns the prebuilt-first source-selection and durable fallback policy.
- This Issue is the concrete product proof consumer. It must not create a second Carry Core or universal OCI framework.

## Closure

Close only when an independent reviewer can state:

> The exact handoff input was rebuilt from its immutable pins into one minimal Nix runtime closure; normal and offline builds agree; the final closure passes version, dependency, conformance, all three real-PTY popup journeys, exact two-pane topology, real Vim-to-HQ submit, one managed-worker result chain, and clean shutdown; the same closure is distributed as Docker and OCI archives; both image paths execute the complete proof and produce semantically matching Receipts; the resulting artifact is downloadable and independently testable under WSLC; and the final source Git bundle contains only the bounded proof implementation and evidence contract.
