{"body":"## Goal

Close the ADRS self-output and governance final-monitor gap.

The system is complete only when:

1. ADRS owns the accepted output-plane contract.
2. ADRS itself emits required output evidence under that contract.
3. Governance consumes real repo packets through the final gate without becoming meaning authority.
4. Missing, stale, hand-written, malformed, or unclassified outputs fail closed.
5. Each selected repo has exactly one canonical governance output path, and repo-local inputs/outputs are classified as source, adapter, deprecated, or residual.
6. Completion evidence is readable as a buyer/auditor-facing control certificate.

This issue is not complete when issue/PR surfaces merely exist.
It is complete only after merged state, readback, final-gate observation, fail-closed evidence, and cutover evidence exist.

## Parent / refs

Parent:

- Refs #125
- Refs #82

ADRS refs:

- Refs roccho-dev/adrs#130 — governance input adoption
- Refs roccho-dev/adrs#131 — README projection receipts
- Refs roccho-dev/adrs#132 — package inventory / assertions / receipts
- Refs roccho-dev/adrs#133 — local gov-package-output cutover plan

Governance refs:

- Refs #115 — branch protection / ruleset final-gate cutover
- Final gate: `gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate`

Downstream refs:

- Refs roccho-dev/ops#33 — local cutover
- Refs roccho-dev/ui#103 — local cutover

## Problem

Current issue/PR coverage is good, but closure is still distributed.

The risk is that each repo continues to grow its own input/output surfaces while governance observes only partial or shadow evidence. That creates false-green risk:

- ADRS may appear compliant through old local checks while missing full gov-package-output evidence.
- Governance may run selftests or shadow reports without consuming real selected repo packets as merge authority.
- Repo-local artifacts, reports, handoff packets, and receipts may be mistaken for final pass.
- Buyer/auditor readback may require reconstructing intent across many PRs instead of reading one closure certificate.

Existing issues identify many of these gaps, but no single parent issue currently says:

> ADRS owns the output-plane contract; governance enforces it non-authoritatively; every selected repo output is classified; unclassified or missing output fails closed.

## Scope to meta

| Level | Purpose | This issue contributes by |
|---:|---|---|
| P0 | Stop ADRS self-output gap | ADRS emits accepted output contract and own packet evidence |
| P1 | Stop gov monitor gap | gov final gate reads real selected repo packets |
| P2 | Stop repo I/O sprawl | every repo output is canonical / adapter / deprecated / residual |
| P3 | Stop false green | reports, artifacts, handoff packets, selftests cannot be final pass |
| P4 | Make merge authority explicit | required check points to final gate only after same-name green evidence |
| P5 | Make closure machine-readable | completion certificate records packet, source, digest, gate, drift |
| P6 | Make audit cheap | buyer can inspect one certificate and linked packet rows |
| P7 | Make org scalable | future repos plug into the same packet contract |
| P8 | Make software asset defensible | evidence path is reproducible and fail-closed |
| P9 | Raise company value | governance system becomes a reusable quality-control asset |
| P10 | Support high-value company sale | technical control plane is legible, low-risk, and transferable |

## Current known evidence

Known good surfaces:

- `governance#125` defines selected real package closure as selected ADRS obligations, selected repo package inventory, and selected package responses joining with zero blocking drift under the governance strict gate.
- `governance#82` requires strict final gate behavior, same-name green evidence, branch protection cutover, CI intent cutover, and old CI demotion.
- `governance#115` targets ruleset / branch protection cutover to the final gate after same-name green evidence exists.
- `adrs#132` correctly states that the authority repo must not be exempt from package-level closure and that final org admission must not be claimed before accepted decision refs and real CI evidence digests exist.

Known remaining gaps:

- `adrs#131`, `adrs#132`, and `adrs#133` remain open/draft or blocked surfaces.
- `adrs#133` is explicitly a blocked plan only and does not alter workflows, branch protection, or required checks.
- final-gate cutover and downstream local cutovers remain blockers under `governance#125`.

## Required closure model

### Authority split

| Actor | Owns | Must not own |
|---|---|---|
| ADRS | accepted meaning, output contract, package obligations | downstream runtime truth |
| Governance | packet verification, final join, gate result, branch-protection intent | accepted meaning authority |
| Each repo | local source evidence and producer adapter | final org admission |
| Final gate | merge authority after cutover | semantic authorship |

### Output classification

Every selected repo output must be classified as one of:

| Class | Meaning | Allowed final-pass role |
|---|---|---|
| canonical | required `govPackageOutput.v1` or accepted equivalent | yes |
| source | input used to build canonical packet | no, unless packeted |
| adapter | local translation into canonical packet | no standalone pass |
| producer | artifact/check/report producer | no standalone pass |
| selftest | tool regression proof | no standalone pass |
| deprecated | kept temporarily with removal or demotion plan | no |
| residual | known gap with owner and next action | no |

Unclassified output is blocking drift.

## Deliverables

### D1. ADRS accepted output-plane contract

Add or link an accepted ADRS record that defines:

- canonical output packet kind;
- required packet files;
- required row kinds;
- required source/digest/provenance fields;
- required package inventory / assertion / receipt coverage;
- README projection receipt expectations;
- allowed non-authority boundaries;
- how local checks may or may not claim compliance.

Completion requires accepted refs/digests, not proposal-only refs.

### D2. ADRS self-packet closure

ADRS must emit its own packet evidence:

- governance input lock;
- README projection receipts;
- package inventory rows;
- package assertion rows;
- package receipt rows;
- local cutover evidence or explicit blocked residual;
- producer provenance;
- readback document.

ADRS is not allowed to be exempt because it is the authority repo.

### D3. Governance real-packet final monitor

Governance final gate must consume real selected repo packet registry rows.

It must fail on:

- missing packet source;
- missing packet path;
- malformed packet;
- hand-written packet;
- stale source revision;
- producer repo mismatch;
- producer revision mismatch;
- packet digest mismatch;
- output digest mismatch;
- missing package inventory;
- missing package assertion;
- missing package receipt;
- non-active admission;
- README drift;
- provider CI drift;
- unclassified repo output;
- expired waiver.

Selftest-only green is not enough.

### D4. Repo output-sprawl burn-down

For each selected repo, produce an output classification table:

| repo | output surface | class | final-pass role | owner | next action |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| governance | final gate packet/report surfaces | canonical / producer / selftest | only final gate may pass | governance | classify all |
| adrs | ADR docs, gov inputs, package rows, local cutover docs | canonical / source / residual | packet only | adrs | close #131/#132/#133 chain |
| ops | ops package closure outputs and local cutover | canonical / adapter / residual | packet only | ops | close local cutover after #115 |
| ui | UI package outputs, preview evidence, local cutover | canonical / adapter / residual | packet only | ui | resolve selected blocker |
| hq | rows/proofs/artifacts | source / producer / residual unless selected | no final pass unless selected | hq | classify or exclude explicitly |

Acceptance requires zero unclassified selected outputs.

### D5. Final cutover certificate

Add a single completion certificate that includes:

- selected universe digest;
- packet registry digest;
- ADRS output contract ref/digest;
- final gate check name;
- branch protection / ruleset ref;
- old CI demotion ref;
- per-repo packet outcome;
- per-repo output-sprawl count;
- residual count;
- waiver count;
- rollback ref;
- final result.

The certificate must be human-readable and machine-readable.

## Acceptance criteria

Close this issue only when all are true:

1. ADRS accepted output contract exists and is linked by digest.
2. ADRS own gov-package-output packet exists with README receipt, package inventory, package assertion, and package receipt rows.
3. Governance final gate reads real selected repo packet sources, not only fixtures or selftests.
4. Missing / stale / malformed / hand-written / digest-mismatched packet evidence fails.
5. Every selected repo output is classified.
6. Unclassified selected output count is zero.
7. Blocking drift count is zero, or every residual has accepted waiver with owner and expiry.
8. Same-name `gov-final-scope-purpose-join / gate` has green evidence before ruleset cutover.
