11. ADRS local cutover no longer allows old local checks to imply final compliance.
12. Ops and UI local cutovers are either complete or explicitly residual with accepted owner/expiry.
13. Completion certificate exists and links all evidence.
14. Governance remains non-authority over accepted meaning.
15. Buyer/auditor can read the certificate and understand what is enforced, what is only evidence, and what remains residual.

## Not done when

This issue is not complete when:

- issue exists but no merged PR exists;
- PR exists but is draft / blocked;
- PR is merged but no readback exists;
- final gate runs selftest only;
- shadow report is generated but not required;
- artifact output is green but not joined;
- handoff packet exists but selected repo packet is missing;
- local repo checks remain able to imply final compliance;
- branch protection points to old CI;
- selected repo output surfaces remain unclassified;
- governance claims meaning authority.

