- final-gate cutover and downstream local cutovers remain blockers under `governance#125`.

## Required closure model

### Authority split

| Actor | Owns | Must not own |
|---|---|---|
| ADRS | accepted meaning, output contract, package obligations | downstream runtime truth |
| Governance | packet verification, final join, gate result, branch-protection intent | accepted meaning authority |
| Each repo | local source evidence and producer adapter | final org admission |
| Final gate | merge authority after cutover | semantic authorship |

### Output classification

Every selected repo output must be classified as one of:

| Class | Meaning | Allowed final-pass role |
|---|---|---|
| canonical | required `govPackageOutput.v1` or accepted equivalent | yes |
| source | input used to build canonical packet | no, unless packeted |
| adapter | local translation into canonical packet | no standalone pass |
| producer | artifact/check/report producer | no standalone pass |
| selftest | tool regression proof | no standalone pass |
